## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant degradation control in real-time multi-hop pipelines under load.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health propagation across hops
- Per-tenant circuit-breakers and edge state
- Minute-by-minute control loops with queue depth and SLA awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example control logic sketch (pseudo)
type TenantState = { id:string; ckne:string; queue:number; sla:'high'|'medium'|'low'; mode:'OPEN'|'HALF'|'CLOSED' };
function tick(states:TenantState[]) {
  for (const s of states){
    const th = s.sla==='high'? 100: s.sla==='medium'? 60: 40;
    if (s.ckne === 'red' || s.queue > th) s.mode = 'OPEN';
    else if (s.ckne === 'yellow') s.mode = 'HALF';
    else s.mode = 'CLOSED';
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-aware, policy-driven enforcement in a multi-tenant setting with privacy constraints.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE maps to latency budgets, sampling rates, and audit retention
- Minute-by-minute degradation loop with fair reallocation
- Payload shape and telemetry for validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: compute quotas based on CKNE
function quotasByCKNE(ckne) {
  const base = 100;
  const latencyBudget = base * (1 - ckne);
  const maskingRate = 1 - 0.8 * ckne;
  const retentionDays = Math.max(1, 7 - Math.floor(6 * ckne));
  return { latencyBudget, maskingRate, retentionDays };
}
```

